    "sha256": "674b8d8f6dd0b8daad20f81daf7cda71abe331475377818968b236354e6c09ef",
    "source": "Figure 21(a), printed page 46, PDF page index 55. Values transcribed from the numerical labels, not digitized from the curves.",
    "quantity": "Pressure-derived section lift and quarter-chord pitching-moment coefficients; reported to two decimal places.",
    "conditions": {
      "alpha_deg": 4,
      "Re_chord": 1500000,
      "chord_ft": 1.7,
      "semi_span_ft": 5.59,
      "tip": "square",
      "wall_correction": "not applied to the reported measurements"
    },
    "notes": [
      "The report infers LE pressure from a thin-airfoil ellipse model and TE pressure from averaged linear extrapolations, then integrates expanded pressure data. These are experimental pressure-derived loads, not direct balance measurements.",
      "Free-air inviscid calculations omit tunnel-wall, boundary-layer and wake-roll-up effects. A rounded-tip calculation is also shown; it is not the same experimental geometry.",
      "Candidate8 flat-cap diagnostic falls back to span-quadratic doublets. Its rounded-tip case uses tensor-quadratic doublets. This comparison does not isolate geometry from numerical-method changes.",
      "Section pitching moment is positive nose-up about quarter chord. Rounding precision is approximately 0.005 per printed coefficient; this is not the measurement uncertainty."
    ],
